content.thinking:
Interesting — two characterization tests failed pre-refactor, revealing my wrong assumptions:

1. "an undeterminable branch fails before any staging" — `makeCli({branch: ''})` → `makeCli` has `if (command === 'git branch --show-current') return options.branch || 'test/PROJ-123';` — `'' || 'test/PROJ-123'` → returns 'test/PROJ-123'! So empty branch can't be simulated with `branch: ''` via makeCli. I need a custom cli returning ''. Fix the test: build cli that returns '' for branch --show-current.

2. "a failing origin fetch warns and the flow continues" — expected truthy got false: `cli.calls.some(c === 'git fetch origin main')` is false. Why? The fetch command: 'git fetch origin ' + baseBranch where baseBranch from REWORK_CONFIG.git.baseBranch = 'main' → 'git fetch origin main'. Hmm — but wait: `cli2.calls = cli.calls` — cli2 pushes into `calls` INSIDE fn closure of makeCli — `var calls = []` inside makeCli; fn pushes there; cli.calls getter — I assigned `cli2.calls = cli.calls` BEFORE any call — assignment copies the array reference at that time (same array object — calls array is mutated in place, so reference stays valid). Hmm, but the wrapper cli2 only pushes via cli(args) — cli pushes into `calls` closure array — same reference. So why false?

OH — `cli.calls` — makeCli does `fn.calls = calls` — cli.calls IS the closure array. `cli2.calls = cli.calls` — fine, same array. The fetch: cli2 intercepts 'git fetch origin main' → THROWS — never reaches cli → never recorded in calls! That's the bug in my test: the intercepted command never gets pushed. Fix: push the command into cli.calls before throwing:

```js
var cli2 = function(args) {
   cli.calls.push(args.command);
   if (args.command === 'git fetch origin main') throw new Error('fetch boom');
   return cli(args);
};
``

Wait but then subsequent assertions on cli.calls also include the pushed one. Good.

Also for 'a rejected push escalates': passed ✓ (because the push rejection path pushes... wait it asserted forced push was called — cli(args) wasn't reached for the rejected command but the forced one was. OK).

Also for the fetch test the throw happens INSIDE commitAndPush's try → warn → continue ✓.

3. Also makeCli({branch:'main'}) worked because 'main' is truthy. ✓ ('pushing directly to main' passed.)

Now — characterization test for "an undeterminable branch": build a custom cli:

```js
var calls = [];
var cli = function(args) {
   calls.push(args.command);
   if (args.command === 'git branch --show-current') return '';
   if (args.command.indexOf('git rev-parse --quiet --verify MERGE_HEAD') !== -1) throw new Error('no merge');
   if (args.command.indexOf('git ls-remote --heads origin') === 0) return SHA40 + '\trefs/heads/test/PROJ-123';
   if (args.command === 'git rev-parse HEAD') return SHA40;
